WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.890
It's Sunday, November 15, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.300
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in superintelligence.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.830
Today's about the human touch.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.110
Elon Musk says Nvidia's big deals were a handshake with Jensen Huang.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.360
Without him, Musk warns, some of those deals will be lost.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.500
Meanwhile,

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.230
Google's Gemini 4 Carbon just took first place on a tough math leaderboard.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:43.000
Anthropic's Claude came second. OpenAI, the long-time leader, slipped to third.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.270
It isn't cheap, though: about fifteen times the cost per run.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.090
In New Delhi,

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:53.990
cancer doctor Siddhartha Mukherjee said AI cuts early drug discovery from eight years to a few months.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.650
But trials, he said, still run on the regulator's clock.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.220
Now, the people.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:06.890
Anthropic's seven co-founders could soon be worth about $17 billion each.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.940
Britain's Treasury is reportedly war-gaming a tax on AI,

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.900
in case it takes too many jobs.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.910
Next week, Trump and Xi are set to talk about a hotline for AI emergencies.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.370
And in India,

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:28.350
Karnataka is adding AI classes for ninth graders in 1,800 public schools.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.090
This week in Perth,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:36.250
a CSIRO team checked the first-ever black hole photo with an AI trained on cats and dogs.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.890
It had never seen a black hole,

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.990
so it couldn't be biased. It found the same ring.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.780
The catch? In Edinburgh,

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:51.090
about 6,000 people marched against giant AI data centres.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.400
And four nonprofits are suing to freeze AI at this week's level.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.150
Back to the machines. Tesla's inviting some buyers to own a Cybercab,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.640
with no steering wheel.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:15.930
It's $29,990, plus $299 a month. Even Musk calls that too high.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:21.030
This week, Runway turned a video AI into a robot brain, and gave it away free.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.040
That's the human touch. Machines keep getting smarter,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.380
but trust still starts with a handshake.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
